// 7-doctype matrix): these 26 states never made it into that matrix, so
// instead of building all 7 doc types for each (182 more pages), each
// state gets ONE spotlight page for whichever document type actually
// fits its economy/culture — Wyoming gets a vehicle bill of sale page,
// not a wedding-planner one, Delaware gets an NDA page, and so on. Four
// states (Kentucky, Louisiana, Oklahoma, Oregon — the largest by
// population among the 26) get a second page with a different doc type.
//
// The brief for this batch: the hero (H1 + subheading) must evoke the
// state WITHOUT literally naming it — see heroAccentEn/Es and
// heroSubtitleEn/Es on DocTypeState, added specifically for this file.
// The rest of the page (meta title, meta description, IncludedCards
// heading, FAQ heading) still names the state normally, which is
// unchanged behavior in DocTypeStateLanding and good for local SEO.
//
// No real per-state sales data exists in this app's schema to decide
// which doc type "sells most" per state (checked sign_transactions,
// documents, analytics_visitors — none tie a US state to a document-type
// purchase), so each assignment below is a reasoned pick based on that
// state's known economy/demographics, not analytics.

